From 0cebf8d278adaa5800ac607e0c65e9d48765aead Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:47:27 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] camera: port the HALv1 client to the Android 15 QPR2
 camera service

LineageOS 22.2 (android-15.0.0_r32) reworked the camera service client
interface. Adapt the HALv1 CameraClient and HidlDeviceInfo1 to it:

- CameraClient takes the AttributionAndPermissionUtils, the client's
  AttributionSourceState, the calling pid and the rotation override, and
  passes them to the new CameraService::Client constructor.
- CameraThreadState is gone; the calling pid/uid come from the client's
  own attribution utils. mClientPid became mCallingPid, and the uid and
  package name are read through getClientUid() / getPackageName().
- startCameraOps() is now notifyCameraOpening().
- Preview, preview-callback and video targets are SurfaceType; the
  HALv1 path still works on the IGraphicBufferProducer, taken from it
  with flagtools::surfaceTypeToIGBP().
- notifyClientSharedAccessPriorityChanged() is a no-op: camera sharing
  is a camera2-only feature.
- HidlDeviceInfo1::getCameraInfo() takes the rotationOverride mode that
  replaced the portrait override flag.
